---
import DirectoryLayout from "../layouts/DirectoryLayout.astro";
import SafetyNotice from "../components/SafetyNotice.astro";
---

<DirectoryLayout
  heading="Job Seeker Safety & Scam Guide"
  subheading="Essential safety practices for discovering and evaluating job openings in public online communities."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "All Jobs", item: "/jobs" },
    { name: "Safety Guide", item: "/safety" },
  ]}
  canonicalPath="/safety"
  pageType="trust"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base font-medium text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
    <SafetyNotice type="job-warning" />

    <!-- Core Rule 1 -->
    <section class="neo-card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 bg-white">
      <div class="inline-block bg-[#FECDD3] px-2 py-0.5 border-2 border-black text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider shadow-[1.5px_1.5px_0px_0px_#000]">
        RED FLAG #1
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-black">
        1. Never Pay for a Job, Equipment, or Application Fee
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Legitimate employers will never ask candidates to pay money upfront.</strong> Beware of:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-700 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <li>"Application processing fees" or "background check fees".</li>
        <li>"Software training deposits" or "home office kit setup fees".</li>
        <li>Wire transfers, gift cards, Zelle/CashApp requests, or cryptocurrency transactions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Core Rule 2 -->
    <section class="neo-card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 bg-white">
      <div class="inline-block bg-[#FEF08A] px-2 py-0.5 border-2 border-black text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider shadow-[1.5px_1.5px_0px_0px_#000]">
        RED FLAG #2
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-black">
        2. Beware of "Task Optimization" & Crypto Deposit Schemes
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        A common online fraud involves offering lucrative daily pay ($200–$500/day) for simple tasks like rating hotel apps, clicking products, or watching videos:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-700 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <li>They allow small withdrawals at first to build trust.</li>
        <li>Then they require "recharging" account balances with USDT/crypto to continue or withdraw larger sums.</li>
        <li>Any job requiring you to deposit money to unlock tasks is 100% fraudulent.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Core Rule 3 -->
    <section class="neo-card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 bg-white">
      <div class="inline-block bg-[#BAE6FD] px-2 py-0.5 border-2 border-black text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider shadow-[1.5px_1.5px_0px_0px_#000]">
        RED FLAG #3
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-black">
        3. Verify Email Domains & Recruiter Identities
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        Scammers frequently impersonate recognizable companies (e.g. Amazon, Google, Microsoft, Shopify):
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-700 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <li>Real corporate recruiters use company email domains (e.g. <code>@company.com</code>), not generic <code>@gmail.com</code>, <code>@telegram.me</code>, or lookalike misspelled domains.</li>
        <li>Legitimate corporate interviews do not take place solely via text chat without video or voice verification.</li>
        <li>Always cross-check open vacancies on the employer's official careers portal.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Core Rule 4 -->
    <section class="neo-card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 bg-white">
      <div class="inline-block bg-[#DDD6FE] px-2 py-0.5 border-2 border-black text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-wider shadow-[1.5px_1.5px_0px_0px_#000]">
        RED FLAG #4
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-black">
        4. Protect Sensitive Identity Information
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        Do not provide sensitive identification data during initial chat conversations:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-700 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <li>Social Security Numbers (SSN), National Insurance (NI) numbers, Social Insurance Numbers (SIN), or Tax File Numbers (TFN).</li>
        <li>Bank account logins, credit card numbers, or copies of government photo IDs prior to receiving a formal verified offer letter through official company systems.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Report CTA -->
    <div class="rounded-3xl border-[3px] border-black bg-[#FEF08A] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-[6px_6px_0px_0px_#000] flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-black text-black">Found a Suspicious Job Community?</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-black/80">
          Help protect fellow job seekers by reporting scam channels or fee-charging groups for immediate removal.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a
        href="/report"
        class="neo-btn bg-[#FECDD3] hover:bg-[#FDA4AF] text-black px-4 py-2.5 text-xs font-black shrink-0 border-2 border-black shadow-[2px_2px_0px_0px_#000]"
      >
        Report a Suspicious Group &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DirectoryLayout>
